  <sharedRules>
    <rule id="bee1-da2a-71d1-20db" name="Israelite (AoA2) - List Notes" publicationId="fcb9-17be-94c2-bcfc" hidden="false">
      <description>ARMIES OF ANTIQUITY v2 #118 (unofficial, Martin Gibbins). This list depicts the army of Israel from the formation of the state until its conquest by Babylon. Early armies fought in upland regions and do not include chariots. Allies And Mercenaries: Any army may take allies from the Arab Nomad list. Late Armies only:

ARMY COMPOSITIONS (pick one in the Army composition list):
[Israelite - Early Army 1200 BC to 1000 BC]
  Allies and Mercenaries: up to 25%
  Characters: up to 33%
  Infantry: at least 25%
  Characters: up to 33% Infantry: At least 25% Allies &amp; Mercenaries: up to 25%
[Israelite - Later Army 1000 BC to 600 BC]
  Allies and Mercenaries: up to 50%
  Characters: up to 25%
  Chariotry and Cavalry: up to 50%
  Infantry: at least 25%
  Characters: up to 25% Chariotry and Cavalry: up to 50% Infantry: At least 25% Allies &amp; Mercenaries: up to 50%</description>
    </rule>
  </sharedRules>
</catalogue>
